(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #108: the runtime ownership flag in action, not the
 static gate - `t`'s first value is a literal (rodata), so its owned flag
 must be 0 and the first `Set` must skip freeing (freeing `.rodata` would
 be its own memory-safety fault, worse than the leak this fix closes). The
 SECOND `Set` reads a flag that IS 1 (the first Set's own format-string
 result), so it frees that intermediate string - the actual fix exercised,
 not just its safety rail.)

a text called t is "hello".
Set t to "{t}!".
Set t to "{t}?".
Print t.
